{"name":"Sweet Dreams","hex":"#eccee5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet dreams","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Phrase","definitions":["Said to someone before they fall asleep, wishing them a good sleep."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet_dreams"}],"entries":[{"title":"Okay Bill","blocks":[{"text":"Okay Bill is a 1971 film directed by John G. Avildsen. The film was also released under the title Sweet Dreams."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/Okay_Bill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Okay_Bill"},{"title":"Sweet Dreams (1981 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sweet Dreams is a 1981 Italian comedy-drama film directed, written and starring Nanni Moretti.\nIt entered the 38th Venice International Film Festival, in which won the Special Jury Prize."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ea/Sogni_d%27oro_%281981_Film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_Dreams_(1981_film)"},{"title":"Sweet Dreams (Are Made of This)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sweet Dreams (Are Made of This)\" is a song by the British synth-pop duo Eurythmics. It was released in January 1983 by RCA Records as the fourth and final single from their second album, Sweet Dreams (Are Made of This) (1983). It was Eurythmics' breakthrough hit, establishing them worldwide. It reached number two on the UK singles chart in March 1983 and number one on the US Billboard Hot 100 six months later; it was the first Eurythmics single released in the US."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/00/Eurythmics_SDAMOT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_Dreams_(Are_Made_of_This)"},{"title":"Sweetness","blocks":[{"text":"Sweetness is a basic taste most commonly perceived when eating foods rich in sugar. Sweet tastes are generally regarded as pleasurable. In addition to sugars like sucrose, many other chemical compounds are sweet, including aldehydes, ketones, and sugar alcohols. Some are sweet at very low concentrations, allowing their use as non-caloric sugar substitutes. Such non-sugar sweeteners include saccharin, aspartame, sucralose and stevia. Other compounds, such as miraculin, may alter perception of sweetness itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Strawberry_shortcake.jpg/330px-Strawberry_shortcake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweetness"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Movement_Computer_Systems_%28MCS%29_Drum_System_II_%28or_Percussion_Computer_II%29%2C_circa_1981%2C_United_Kingdom_-_Knobcon_2014.jpg/500px-Movement_Computer_Systems_%28MCS%29_Drum_System_II_%28or_Percussion_Computer_II%29%2C_circa_1981%2C_United_Kingdom_-_Knobcon_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Movement_Computer_Systems_%28MCS%29_Drum_System_II_%28or_Percussion_Computer_II%29%2C_circa_1981%2C_United_Kingdom_-_Knobcon_2014.jpg/500px-Movement_Computer_Systems_%28MCS%29_Drum_System_II_%28or_Percussion_Computer_II%29%2C_circa_1981%2C_United_Kingdom_-_Knobcon_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stewart used a Movement Systems Drum Computer which also makes an appearance in the music video","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMovement_Computer_Systems_(MCS)_Drum_System_II_(or_Percussion_Computer_II)%2C_circa_1981%2C_United_Kingdom_-_Knobcon_2014.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/BBC_Television_Centre.JPG/500px-BBC_Television_Centre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb